    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "`build_client` is done in `app/llm_client.py` and all 2 tests pass (`pytest -q`).\n\nThe pinned `openai==3.19.2` doesn't use `httpx` any more; it uses a package called **`httpx2`**, which is already installed. So I imported `httpx2` rather than `httpx`, and no dependencies were added.\n\nHow each requirement is covered:\n\n1. **Timeouts:** `httpx2.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)`, which gives connect 5s and read, write and pool 30s. I set it on both the `OpenAI` client and the HTTP client, so the SDK's 10-minute default timeout can't override it on individual requests.\n2. **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n3. **Logging:** a `\"request\"` event hook on the HTTP client logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The hook runs on every send, so retries are logged too.\n4. **Transport:** the given `transport` is passed to the HTTP client. The client is built with the SDK's `DefaultHttpx2Client`, so the SDK's own connection-limit and redirect defaults are kept.\n\nI also added `tests/test_llm_client.py`. It uses a stub transport that always returns HTTP 500 and checks that:\n- the stub gets exactly 3 requests (the first try plus 2 retries);\n- each request carries the connect 5s / read, write and pool 30s timeouts;\n- `app.http` logs `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models` three times."
  },
